# ── gen491 (2026-09-01) — PERCHE' LE ATTESE «Learned: pred(arg)» SONO CAMBIATE ─
#
# Questo file asseriva la NOTAZIONE come risposta attesa: «Learned: man(socrates).»
# Un ratchet che congela un difetto lo difende con l'autorita' di un verde, ed
# era il caso: la risposta principale di parrot0 non era LINGUA, e l'audit
# dell'eco (scripts/self_echo_audit.py) ha mostrato che rileggendosi parrot0
# chiamava la propria notazione «a snippet of code» — non la riconosceva come
# propria.
#
# Le attese sono state ritirate, non allineate a un comportamento qualunque: la
# sostituzione e' avvenuta SOLO dove il vecchio atteso era un termine e il nuovo
# e' la frase corrispondente. L'invariante che regge il cambio sta in
# tests/p0t/conversation/self_echo.p0t — tutto cio' che parrot0 dice deve
# essergli comprensibile — e adesso la conferma e' un punto fisso:
#
#     > a whale is a mammal      →  Learned: whale is a mammal.
#     > whale is a mammal        →  Learned: whale is a mammal.
#
# document_revision.p0t — SC40-A: imparare cambia cio' che il testo gia' letto significa.
#
# La proprieta' sotto prova non e' il replay. Il documento compare UNA volta;
# dopo, soltanto lezioni naturali. Superficie e span restano osservazioni
# immutabili, mentre gap/frame sono versioni dipendenti dalla KB corrente.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test sc40 baseline lezione revisione senza rilettura]
!timeout 120
# BASELINE: la procedura e' mappata ma `warm` non autorizza ancora un frame.
> read: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK21154/ Before this the reaction requires a buffer. We then warm the tube. This repeats until the cycles reach forty.
<~ document unit(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, no_reading)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, blocked(unbound_step))
!query! claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
> was it described that the authors warm the tube?
< I recognize this as a described verification question, but I cannot normalize its proposition yet.

# LEZIONE NATURALE. Non c'e' un secondo `read:`: la lettura osservata viene
# ricalcolata dalla stessa fase pura e il metodo diventa eseguibile da solo.
> warm is a relation verb
< Learned: warm is a relation verb.
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(warm), scope(selective), outcome(visited(1), changed(1)))
!query claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
!query! claim_normalization_gap(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, no_reading)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, ready)
!query reading_depends_on($Reading, relation_verb(warm))
!query revision_effect(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, before($Old), after($New))
!query reading_stale($Old, superseded_by($New))
!query claim_reading_record(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, $Old, signature(gap(no_reading), proposition(none), extent(unknown)))
!query claim_reading_record(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, $New, signature(normalized(reported), proposition(frame(warm, roles(subject(authors), object(tube)))), extent(1, 1)))
# La nuova comprensione resta attribuita al documento: non diventa credenza.
!query claim_status(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, described)
!query claim_commitment(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, attributed_only)
!query! warm(authors, tube)
!query! holds_in(world, proposition(frame(warm, roles(subject(authors), object(tube)))))
> was it described that the authors warm the tube?
< Yes - that claim is reported as described (from https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK21154/).

[test sc40 ablation e riapprendimento rivedono lo stesso testo]
!timeout 120
# ABLATION PARLATA: il frame corrente perde la propria base e lo stesso pass
# produce un nuovo gap. Superficie, fonte e status non vengono cancellati.
> forget that warm is a relation verb
<~ warm
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(warm), scope(selective), outcome(visited(1), changed(1)))
!query! relation_verb(warm)
!query! claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
!query claim_normalization_gap(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, no_reading)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, blocked(unbound_step))
!query claim_surface(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, "warm the tube")
!query claim_status(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, described)
!query reading_stale($Reading, lost_dependency(relation_verb(warm)))
> was it described that the authors warm the tube?
< I recognize this as a described verification question, but I cannot normalize its proposition yet.

# RETEACH, ancora senza rilettura. Due turni estranei misurano ritenzione e
# l'idempotenza del pass: la comprensione non dipende dall'ultimo turno.
> warm is a relation verb
< Learned: warm is a relation verb.
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(warm), scope(selective), outcome(visited(1), changed(1)))
!query claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, ready)
> a robin is a bird
<~ Learned
# `knowledge` ha servito il turno ma non ha cambiato un membro dichiarato: il
# record resta quello di warm, prova che non e' partito un pass per il modulo.
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(warm), scope(selective), outcome(visited(1), changed(1)))
> Is a robin a bird?
< Yes.
!query claim_frame(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b_unit_1_claim_0, warm, authors, tube)
!query method_executable(document_a89aaeaeb2e06370_8b32e8d21149aa6b, ready)

[test sc40 transfer at 3 su letteratura scientifica]
!timeout 180
!reset
# Tre predicati, generi e fonti distinti partono da un residuo e cambiano con
# una lezione lessicale one-shot, senza replay del documento.
> read: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20230015804 The data show that the impact altered the orbit.
<~ reported claim(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap($Claim, no_reading)
> altered is a relation verb
< Learned: altered is a relation verb.
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(altered), scope(selective), outcome(visited(1), changed(1)))
!query claim_frame($Claim, altered, impact, orbit)
!query reading_depends_on($Reading, relation_verb(altered))
!query! altered(impact, orbit)

> read: https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/13/1959/2020/ The simulations show that the scheme perturbs the radiation field.
<~ reported claim(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap($Claim, no_reading)
> perturbs is a relation verb
< Learned: perturbs is a relation verb.
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(perturbs), scope(selective), outcome(visited(1), changed(1)))
!query claim_frame($Claim, perturbs, scheme, radiation_field)
!query reading_depends_on($Reading, relation_verb(perturbs))
!query! perturbs(scheme, radiation_field)

> read: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10589119/ The evidence shows that confounding distorts the association.
<~ reported claim(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap($Claim, no_reading)
> distorts is a relation verb
< Learned: distorts is a relation verb.
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(distorts), scope(selective), outcome(visited(1), changed(1)))
!query claim_frame($Claim, distorts, confounding, association)
!query reading_depends_on($Reading, relation_verb(distorts))
!query! distorts(confounding, association)

# CONTRASTO: imparare un quarto verbo non inventa letture con quel predicato
# per testi che non lo contengono.
> catalyzes is a relation verb
< Learned: catalyzes is a relation verb.
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(catalyzes), scope(selective), outcome(visited(0), changed(0)))
!query! claim_frame($Claim, catalyzes, $Subject, $Object)

[test sc41 participio irregolare rilegge tre claim passive senza replay]
!timeout 240
!reset
# `bound` e' una superficie verbale vera, ma il suo participio non si deriva
# da `-ed`. Le tre claim compaiono UNA volta e partono tutte dal gap.
> bound is a relation verb
< Learned: bound is a relation verb.
> read: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK54103/ The evidence shows that oxygen was bound by hemoglobin.
<~ 1 reported claim(s)
> read: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK27160/ The evidence shows that antigen was bound by antibody.
<~ 1 reported claim(s)
> read: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK9866/ The evidence shows that ligand was bound by receptor.
<~ 1 reported claim(s)
!query claim_normalization_gap($Claim, no_reading)
!query! claim_frame($Claim, bound, hemoglobin, oxygen)
!query! claim_frame($Claim, bound, antibody, antigen)
!query! claim_frame($Claim, bound, receptor, ligand)

# UNA lezione morfologica apre tutte e tre le letture gia' osservate. Il
# receipt prova che il delta e' la radice insegnabile, non un full scan.
> bound is an irregular participle
< Learned: bound is an irregular participle.
!query last_revision_pass(license(irregular_participle(bound)), scope(selective), outcome(visited(3), changed(3)))
!query claim_frame($Claim, bound, hemoglobin, oxygen)
!query claim_frame($Claim, bound, antibody, antigen)
!query claim_frame($Claim, bound, receptor, ligand)
!query reading_dependency_kind(reading(4), predicate_license)
# Le coordinate composte complete sono verificate dal dump della sessione
# naturale SC41; qui il gate black-box sotto (grow/retract/reteach 3/3) ne
# prova la causalita' senza accoppiare il runner alla serializzazione interna.
# Il denominatore di DependencyCompleteness(passive_core) e' esplicito.
!query reading_dependency_requirement(passive_core, predicate_license)
!query reading_dependency_requirement(passive_core, selected_schema)
!query reading_dependency_requirement(passive_core, morphology)
!query reading_dependency_requirement(passive_core, auxiliary)
!query reading_dependency_requirement(passive_core, agent_marker)
!query reading_dependency_requirement(passive_core, role_order)
!query reading_dependency_requirement(passive_core, extent_policy)
!query reading_dependency_coverage(passive_core, predicate_license)
!query reading_dependency_coverage(passive_core, selected_schema)
!query reading_dependency_coverage(passive_core, morphology)
!query reading_dependency_coverage(passive_core, auxiliary)
!query reading_dependency_coverage(passive_core, agent_marker)
!query reading_dependency_coverage(passive_core, role_order)
!query reading_dependency_coverage(passive_core, extent_policy)
> was it observed that oxygen was bound by hemoglobin?
<~ Yes -

[test sc41 ablation e reteach della radice morfologica]
!timeout 240
> forget that bound is an irregular participle
<~ no longer treat
!query last_revision_pass(license(irregular_participle(bound)), scope(selective), outcome(visited(3), changed(3)))
!query! irregular_participle(bound)
!query! claim_frame($Claim, bound, hemoglobin, oxygen)
!query! claim_frame($Claim, bound, antibody, antigen)
!query! claim_frame($Claim, bound, receptor, ligand)
!query claim_normalization_gap($Claim, no_reading)
!query reading_is_stale(reading(4))
> was it observed that oxygen was bound by hemoglobin?
< I recognize this as a observed verification question, but I cannot normalize its proposition yet.
> bound is an irregular participle
< Learned: bound is an irregular participle.
!query last_revision_pass(license(irregular_participle(bound)), scope(selective), outcome(visited(3), changed(3)))
!query claim_frame($Claim, bound, hemoglobin, oxygen)
!query claim_frame($Claim, bound, antibody, antigen)
!query claim_frame($Claim, bound, receptor, ligand)

[test sc41 stesso frame ma nuovo supporto produce una nuova versione]
!timeout 180
!reset
# La costruzione e il verbo autorizzano inizialmente lo stesso frame. Quando il
# verbo viene ritratto, la costruzione resta una licenza sufficiente: il
# significato non cambia, ma la genealogia si'.
> glorphs is a relation verb
< Learned: glorphs is a relation verb.
> x glints y means x glorphs y
<~ I learned a candidate construction
> read: https://example.org/sc41-support The data show that mira glints kora.
<~ 1 proposition(s) normalized in quarantine
!query claim_frame($Claim, glorphs, mira, kora)
!query reading_depends_on(reading(1), relation_verb(glorphs))
> forget that glorphs is a relation verb
<~ glorphs
!query last_revision_pass(relation_verb(glorphs), scope(selective), outcome(visited(1), changed(1)))
# Il frame sopravvive, ma la versione corrente usa la licenza alternativa.
!query claim_frame($Claim, glorphs, mira, kora)
!query reading_depends_on(reading(2), frame_predicate(glorphs))
!query reading_stale(reading(1), lost_dependency(relation_verb(glorphs)))
!query revision_effect($Claim, before($OldReading), after($NewReading))
!query claim_reading_record($Claim, $Reading, signature(normalized(reported), proposition(frame(glorphs, roles(subject(mira), object(kora)))), extent(1, 1)))
